    `selenium-pw-migrator remediation evaluate --before-run <before> --after-run <after> --candidate "<label>" --autonomy-state migration/state/autonomy-state.json --out migration/state/remediation-evaluation.json`.
 6. Record only that Core decision with `migration/scripts/update-autonomy-state.ps1 -Action RecordCycle -Workspace migration -EvaluationPath migration/state/remediation-evaluation.json`. Never pass an agent-authored `PROGRESS`, `NO_PROGRESS`, `BLOCKED`, metric summary, or candidate fingerprint.
 7. `ACCEPT` is the only progress decision. Core requires at least one deterministic defect/build improvement and rejects measured regressions. Reset `noProgressStreak` and continue automatically while budget remains.
-8. `REJECT_NO_PROGRESS` or `REJECT_REGRESSION` sets `rollbackRequired=true`: restore the complete bounded change before selecting a different independent candidate. Do not carry a rejected patch into the next baseline.
+8. `REJECT_NO_PROGRESS` or `REJECT_REGRESSION` sets `rollbackRequired=true`: restore the complete bounded change, then try a different independent candidate. Do not carry a rejected patch into the next baseline.
 9. `REJECT_CYCLE` stops immediately with `REMEDIATION_CYCLE_DETECTED`. State hashes survive fresh invocation budgets, so `continue` cannot hide an A→B→A loop.
-10. Stop with `STOPPED_TWO_CONSECUTIVE_NO_PROGRESS` after two consecutive rejected cycles on distinct Core-generated candidate fingerprints. At five completed cycles, emit `AUTONOMOUS_CYCLE_BUDGET_REACHED`; `continuous` may roll to another batch, but state history remains.
+10. Stop with `STOPPED_TWO_CONSECUTIVE_NO_PROGRESS` after two consecutive rejected cycles on distinct candidate fingerprints generated by Core. At five completed cycles, emit `AUTONOMOUS_CYCLE_BUDGET_REACHED`; `continuous` may roll to another batch, but state history remains.
 
